    "notes": {
      "item": "Thomson's own words (OR I-2 p. 596), quoted and attributed: a private citizen's advice, not a holder's. His call to make Baltimore 'pay all damages' is his alone, never the narrator's, and no option or effect acts on it (a collective penalty stays outside any lever: SENSITIVE-HISTORY 3.6, R6). Event, no effects."
